{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>וינח</b> Two times in the Masorah: וינח בכל גבול מצרים and וינח ביום השביעי — teaches that the locusts rested on Shabbat. Another interpretation: a hint to that which is stated in Ta'anit: they sound the alarm and fast over locusts on a weekday but not on Shabbat, and this is what is said: וינח בכל גבול מצרים — even if the locusts rested in the entire territory, nonetheless וינח ביום השביעי."], :book :exodus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:12:22.795154832Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}